module j3.gfx.bvh
    Bounding volume hierarchy over triangles, for ray tracing on the GPU (see `gfx.traceMeshes`,
    and `scene3d.traceObjects`, which builds one over object boxes).
    Splits the longest centroid axis where the surface area heuristic says rays test the
    fewest triangles (12 bins), falling back to halving the list.
    Any thread: no module state, so a worker can use a value it owns (`j3c doc threads`).

const LEAF: int = 4
    Triangles in a leaf, at most.

const NODE_FLOATS: int = 8
    Floats per node: `lo.xyz`, first triangle (leaf) or left child (inner), `hi.xyz`,
    triangle count (0 for an inner node, whose right child is left + 1).

struct Bvh
    nodes: []f32
    count: int
    order: []int
        Triangle indices in leaf order; a leaf covers `order[first..first + count]`.
    depth: int
        Levels below the root; the GPU tracer skips subtrees deeper than 45.

fn build(corners: []f32, n: int, arena: &Arena): Bvh
    Build over `n` triangles whose corners are `corners[t * 9 .. t * 9 + 9]`.
